PAOFLOW examples

Cases: ./cases/  (start here)

- One folder per calculation: the Quantum ESPRESSO inputs, a README and case.json (the workflow
  of paoflow-gen and the answers of its form). The pseudopotentials live once in
  ../PSEUDOS/library and are copied in with the case.
- PAOFLOW Studio: Setup tab, "Examples...", pick a case and a folder: Studio copies it, fills the
  form and lists the QE runs in the Runs tab. Command line: `paoflow-gen --example <name>`
  (`paoflow-gen --example list` shows the cases).
- Property runs: si_bands_transport, al_dos_transport, pt_spin_polarized (nspin = 2),
  fe_anomalous_hall, pt_spin_hall, alp_hubbard_optics (Hubbard shifts + dielectric tensor),
  pt_adhoc_soc (ad hoc spin-orbit), snte_spin_texture (2D), mop2_weyl_points,
  gaas_doped_transport (doping and scattering models), te_rashba_edelstein,
  bi_ribbon_edge_states (site-projected bands), bi_bilayer_z2 (Z2 invariant), pt_slab_layer_shc
  (layer-resolved spin Hall), si_optics (dielectric function, JDOS), snte_mirror_chern,
  pd_spin_susceptibility.
- Landauer transport: al_bulk_landauer, alh_junction_landauer (eigenchannels).
- ACBN0 / eACBN0: gaas_acbn0, mgo_acbn0, mno_acbn0 (antiferromagnetic), si_acbn0, zno_acbn0.
- The reference outputs of the cases are in the integration-test tarballs (the releases tagged
  integration-assets-*), not in the repository.

Recipes: ./recipes/

- Scripts for what the generator does not write: VASP runs (recipes/vasp), the basis presets
  on NC and ultrasoft, scalar and fully relativistic pseudopotentials, the sparse backend on a
  doubled cell, the low-level Transport calls of a conductor with a defect.

Electron-phonon coupling: ./elphon/

- One system folder each (system.py, qe/, phonons/, coupling/, superconductivity/, optics/,
  transport/, arpes/): Si (phonon-assisted absorption, emissivity, mobility, ARPES), Pb
  (Eliashberg function, Tc, Migdal-Eliashberg gap, resistivity, infrared optics, ARPES kink),
  MgB2 (anisotropic two-gap Migdal-Eliashberg), SiC (polar crystal: Frohlich coupling,
  quadrupoles, mobility). The same layout is written by `paoflow-gen elphon`.

Non-linear optics: ./nlo_examples/

- Shift current, injection currents and second-harmonic generation: gapped graphene
  (tight-binding model), GaAs (PAW) and monolayer GeS; REPORT.md compares with the literature.

Tight-binding models: ./TBmodel_examples/

- Analytical tight-binding model Hamiltonians (Kane-Mele, graphene, cubium, Slater-Koster);
  the model runs of paoflow-gen / Studio (workflow tb_model) cover the built-in models.

Band unfolding: ./unfold_examples/

- Supercell band structures unfolded to the primitive cell (DFT-PAO and tight-binding)

Quantum oscillations: ./pyskeaf_examples/ and ./qo_analysis_examples/

- Extremal Fermi-surface orbits with pyskeaf (de Haas-van Alphen frequencies and masses) and the
  comparison of the computed frequencies with measured quantum oscillations

The property drivers (main.py, plot.py) of every case are written by paoflow-gen / the Setup tab
of paoflow-studio; the Results and Plots tabs show their outputs. clean_runs.py removes the
outputs of every example folder.
